urity, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-model-strategic-scenarios/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-track-benefit-realization","name_ar":"تتبّع تحقق المنافع","name_en":"Track Benefit Realization","description":"Execute track benefit realization for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to trace promised benefits to evidence, accountable owners, and corrective actions.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Track Benefit Realization\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تتبّع تحقق المنافع  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nTrace promised benefits to evidence, accountable owners, and corrective actions. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-track-benefit-realization/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-review-okr-health","name_ar":"مراجعة صحة مؤشرات OKR","name_en":"Review Okr Health","description":"Execute review okr health for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to test objective quality, key-result integrity, progress confidence, and gaming risk.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Review Okr Health\n\n**الاسم العربي:** مراجعة صحة مؤشرات OKR  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nTest objective quality, key-result integrity, progress confidence, and gaming risk. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-review-okr-health/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-design-operating-model","name_ar":"تصميم نموذج التشغيل","name_en":"Design Operating Model","description":"Execute design operating model for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to define capabilities, decision rights, governance forums, roles, interfaces, and service levels.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Design Operating Model\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تصميم نموذج التشغيل  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nDefine capabilities, decision rights, governance forums, roles, interfaces, and service levels. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-design-operating-model/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-synthesize-crisis-command-brief","name_ar":"صياغة موجز قيادة الأزمة","name_en":"Synthesize Crisis Command Brief","description":"Execute synthesize crisis command brief for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to turn fragmented crisis evidence into priorities, decisions, and a common operating picture.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Synthesize Crisis Command Brief\n\n**الاسم العربي:** صياغة موجز قيادة الأزمة  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nTurn fragmented crisis evidence into priorities, decisions, and a common operating picture. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-synthesize-crisis-command-brief/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-assess-policy-impact","name_ar":"تقييم أثر السياسات","name_en":"Assess Policy Impact","description":"Execute assess policy impact for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to estimate operational, financial, legal, workforce, and technology effects of a proposed policy.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Assess Policy Impact\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تقييم أثر السياسات  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nEstimate operational, financial, legal, workforce, and technology effects of a proposed policy. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-assess-policy-impact/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-prepare-executive-meeting","name_ar":"إعداد اجتماع تنفيذي","name_en":"Prepare Executive Meeting","description":"Execute prepare executive meeting for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to prepare the agenda, decisions required, evidence pack, objections, and follow-through.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Prepare Executive Meeting\n\n**الاسم العربي:** إعداد اجتماع تنفيذي  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nPrepare the agenda, decisions required, evidence pack, objections, and follow-through. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-prepare-executive-meeting/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-challenge-decision-assumptions","name_ar":"اختبار افتراضات القرار","name_en":"Challenge Decision Assumptions","description":"Execute challenge decision assumptions for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to identify fragile assumptions, hidden incentives, missing options, and evidence that could reverse a decision.","category":"executive-strategy","instructions_md":"# Challenge Decision Assumptions\n\n**الاسم العربي:** اختبار افتراضات القرار  \n**المجال:** القيادة والاستراتيجية\n\n## Mission\n\nIdentify fragile assumptions, hidden incentives, missing options, and evidence that could reverse a decision. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- decision objective\n- time horizon\n- trusted KPIs\n- constraints\n- decision owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Frame the decision, owner, deadline, and irreversible consequences.\n2. Separate verified facts, assumptions, forecasts, and stakeholder positions.\n3. Compare at least three viable options against value, risk, feasibility, and timing.\n4. Stress-test the preferred option with a pre-mortem and explicit disconfirming evidence.\n5. Produce a decision record with owner, actions, checkpoints, and leading indicators.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["decision objective","time horizon","trusted KPIs","constraints","decision owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.governance.map-evidence"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-challenge-decision-assumptions/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-analyze-budget-variance","name_ar":"تحليل انحرافات الميزانية","name_en":"Analyze Budget Variance","description":"Execute analyze budget variance for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to explain material budget deviations and distinguish structural issues from timing effects.","category":"finance-procurement","instructions_md":"# Analyze Budget Variance\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تحليل انحرافات الميزانية  \n**المجال:** المالية والمشتريات\n\n## Mission\n\nExplain material budget deviations and distinguish structural issues from timing effects. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- period and currency\n- approved baseline\n- transaction evidence\n- materiality threshold\n- control owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the accounting period, currency, baseline, materiality, and source completeness.\n2. Reconcile totals to authoritative ledgers before interpreting variances.\n3. Segment findings by price, volume, timing, scope, mix, and control failure.\n4. Quantify confidence, downside exposure, and recoverable value.\n5. Recommend controlled actions with owner, approval route, and audit evidence.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.sap.read-purchase-order`\n- `nx.governance.register-risk`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["period and currency","approved baseline","transaction evidence","materiality threshold","control owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.sap.read-purchase-order","nx.governance.register-risk"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-analyze-budget-variance/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger","nx_workforce_planning_director","nx_talent_intelligence_lead","nx_employee_experience_lead","nx_customer_experience_director","nx_service_recovery_lead","nx_communications_director","nx_sustainability_director","nx_procurement_value_director","nx_contract_intelligence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-govern-cloud-finops","name_ar":"حوكمة تكاليف السحابة","name_en":"Govern Cloud Finops","descr