e.\n4. Quantify confidence, downside exposure, and recoverable value.\n5. Recommend controlled actions with owner, approval route, and audit evidence.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.sap.read-purchase-order`\n- `nx.governance.register-risk`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["period and currency","approved baseline","transaction evidence","materiality threshold","control owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.sap.read-purchase-order","nx.governance.register-risk"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-extract-contract-obligations/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_executive_advisor","nx_strategy_portfolio_director","nx_board_briefing_director","nx_enterprise_risk_director","nx_finance_value_director","nx_governance_assurance_director","nx_legal_policy_advisor","nx_transformation_office_director","nx_decision_quality_challenger","nx_workforce_planning_director","nx_talent_intelligence_lead","nx_employee_experience_lead","nx_customer_experience_director","nx_service_recovery_lead","nx_communications_director","nx_sustainability_director","nx_procurement_value_director","nx_contract_intelligence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-detect-invoice-anomalies","name_ar":"كشف شذوذ الفواتير","name_en":"Detect Invoice Anomalies","description":"Execute detect invoice anomalies for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to detect duplicates, split purchases, price variance, unusual timing, and supplier anomalies.","category":"finance-procurement","instructions_md":"# Detect Invoice Anomalies\n\n**الاسم العربي:** كشف شذوذ الفواتير  \n**المجال:** المالية والمشتريات\n\n## Mission\n\nDetect duplicates, split purchases, price variance, unusual timing, and supplier anomalies. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- period and currency\n- approved baseline\n- transaction evidence\n- materiality threshold\n- control owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the accounting period, currency, baseline, materiality, and source completeness.\n2. Reconcile totals to authoritative ledgers before interpreting variances.\n3. Segment findings by price, volume, timing, scope, mix, and control failure.\n4. Quantify confidence, downside exposure, and recoverable value.\n5. Recommend controlled actions with owner, approval route, and audit evidence.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.sap.read-purchase-order`\n- `nx.governance.register-risk`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["period and currency","approved baseline","transaction evidence","materiality threshold","control owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.sap.read-purchase-order","nx.governance.register-risk"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-detect-invoice-anomalies/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-forecast-enterprise-cashflow","name_ar":"توقع التدفق النقدي","name_en":"Forecast Enterprise Cashflow","description":"Execute forecast enterprise cashflow for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to forecast cash inflows, outflows, liquidity buffers, and uncertainty bands.","category":"finance-procurement","instructions_md":"# Forecast Enterprise Cashflow\n\n**الاسم العربي:** توقع التدفق النقدي  \n**المجال:** المالية والمشتريات\n\n## Mission\n\nForecast cash inflows, outflows, liquidity buffers, and uncertainty bands. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- period and currency\n- approved baseline\n- transaction evidence\n- materiality threshold\n- control owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the accounting period, currency, baseline, materiality, and source completeness.\n2. Reconcile totals to authoritative ledgers before interpreting variances.\n3. Seg