ector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-screen-visitor-risk/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-verify-vehicle-access","name_ar":"التحقق من دخول المركبات","name_en":"Verify Vehicle Access","description":"Execute verify vehicle access for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to verify vehicle identity, authorization, cargo context, driver, and zone restrictions.","category":"industrial-security","instructions_md":"# Verify Vehicle Access\n\n**الاسم العربي:** التحقق من دخول المركبات  \n**المجال:** الأمن الصناعي\n\n## Mission\n\nVerify vehicle identity, authorization, cargo context, driver, and zone restrictions. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- site and asset\n- event timeline\n- sensor or access evidence\n- threat context\n- response authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Establish the site, asset, event window, data provenance, and life-safety impact.\n2. Correlate independent signals without treating absence of evidence as proof of safety.\n3. Assign severity using likelihood, consequence, velocity, and control effectiveness.\n4. Recommend the least disruptive safe response and identify required human authority.\n5. Preserve a timestamped evidence chain and define escalation and closure criteria.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.secops.correlate-alerts`\n- `nx.physical.search-cctv-events`\n- `nx.physical.dispatch-patrol`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-verify-vehicle-access/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_industrial_security_commander","nx_physical_security_director","nx_soc_ot_fusion_director","nx_access_intelligence_lead","nx_cctv_intelligence_lead","nx_crisis_response_commander","nx_emergency_management_director","nx_hse_assurance_director","nx_investigations_evidence_lead","nx_pdpl_privacy_officer","nx_nca_ecc_assurance_lead","nx_iso27001_auditor","nx_iso45001_auditor","nx_iso55001_auditor","nx_hcis_compliance_lead","nx_third_party_risk_director","nx_records_governance_lead","nx_internal_audit_director"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-detect-access-anomalies","name_ar":"كشف شذوذ التحكم بالدخول","name_en":"Detect Access Anomalies","description":"Execute detect access anomalies for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to detect impossible travel, unusual time, repeated denials, badge sharing, and privilege misuse.","category":"industrial-security","instructions_md":"# Detect Access Anomalies\n\n**الاسم العربي:** كشف شذوذ التحكم بالدخول  \n**المجال:** الأمن الصناعي\n\n## Mission\n\nDetect impossible travel, unusual ti