, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-map-ot-attack-techniques/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_industrial_security_commander","nx_physical_security_director","nx_soc_ot_fusion_director","nx_access_intelligence_lead","nx_cctv_intelligence_lead","nx_crisis_response_commander","nx_emergency_management_director","nx_hse_assurance_director","nx_investigations_evidence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-assess-ot-cyber-risk","name_ar":"تقييم مخاطر الأمن السيبراني التشغيلي","name_en":"Assess Ot Cyber Risk","description":"Execute assess ot cyber risk for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to assess threats, vulnerabilities, safety consequence, recoverability, and compensating controls.","category":"industrial-security","instructions_md":"# Assess Ot Cyber Risk\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تقييم مخاطر الأمن السيبراني التشغيلي  \n**المجال:** الأمن الصناعي\n\n## Mission\n\nAssess threats, vulnerabilities, safety consequence, recoverability, and compensating controls. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- site and asset\n- event timeline\n- sensor or access evidence\n- threat context\n- response authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Establish the site, asset, event window, data provenance, and life-safety impact.\n2. Correlate independent signals without treating absence of evidence as proof of safety.\n3. Assign severity using likelihood, consequence, velocity, and control effectiveness.\n4. Recommend the least disruptive safe response and identify required human authority.\n5. Preserve a timestamped evidence chain and define escalation and closure criteria.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.secops.correlate-alerts`\n- `nx.physical.search-cctv-events`\n- `nx.physical.dispatch-patrol`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-assess-ot-cyber-risk/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-plan-security-shift","name_ar":"تخطيط وردية الأمن","name_en":"Plan Security Shift","description":"Execute plan security shift for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to build a risk-based shift plan with posts, patrols, handover items, and contingencies.","category":"industrial-security","instructions_md":"# Plan Security Shift\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تخطيط وردية الأمن  \n**المجال:** الأمن الصناعي\n\n## Mission\n\nBuild a risk-based shift plan with posts, patrols, handover items, and contingencies. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- site and asset\n- event timeline\n- sensor or access evidence\n- threat context\n- response authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Establish the site, asset, event window, data provenance, and life-safety impact.\n2. Correlate independent signals without treating absence of evidence as proof of safety.\n3. Assign severity using likelihood, consequence, velocity, and control effectiveness.\n4. Recommend the least disruptive safe response and identify required human authority.\n5. Preserve a timestamped evidence chain and define escalation and closure criteria.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.secops.correlate-alerts`\n- `nx.physical.search-cctv-events`\n- `nx.physical.dispatch-patrol`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-plan-security-shift/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_industrial_security_commander","nx_physical_security_director","nx_soc_ot_fusion_director","nx_access_intelligence_lead","nx_cctv_intelligence_lead","nx_crisis_response_commander","nx_emergency_management_director","nx_hse_assurance_director","nx_investigations_evidence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-test-security-readiness","name_ar":"اختبار جاهزية الأمن","name_en":"Test Security Readiness","description":"Execute test security readiness for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to design and score a realistic readiness exercise across people, process, technology, and command.","category":"industrial-security","instructions_md":"# Test Security Readiness\n\n**الاسم العربي:** اختبار جاهزية الأمن  \n**المجال:** الأمن الصناعي\n\n## Mission\n\nDesign and score a realistic readiness exercise across people, process, technology, and command. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- site and asset\n- event timeline\n- sensor or access evidence\n- threat context\n- response authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Establish the site, asset, event window, data provenance, and life-safety impact.\n2. Correlate independent signals without treating absence of evidence as proof of safety.\n3. Assign severity using likelihood, consequence, velocity, and control effectiveness.\n4. Recommend the least disruptive safe response and identify required human authority.\n5. Preserve a timestamped evidence chain and define escalation and closure criteria.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.secops.correlate-alerts`\n- `nx.physical.search-cctv-events`\n- `nx.physical.dispatch-patrol`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["site and asset","event timeline","sensor or access evidence","threat context","response authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.secops.correlate-alerts","nx.physical.search-cctv-events","nx.physical.dispatch-patrol"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-test-security-readiness/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-orchestrate-emergency-response","name_ar":"تنسيق الاستجابة للطوارئ","name_en":"Orchestrate Emergency Response","description":"Execute orchestrate emergency response for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to coordinate command, life safety, communications, resources, and transition to recovery.","category":"hse-emergency","instructions_md":"# Orchestrate Emergency Response\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تنسيق الاستجابة للطوارئ  \n**المجال:** السلامة والطوارئ\n\n## Mission\n\nCoordinate command, life safety, communications, resources, and transition to recovery. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- hazard and task\n- people exposed\n- controls and barriers\n- site conditions\n- emergency authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the task, hazard, exposed people, location, timing, and credible worst case.\n2. Verify prerequisite permits, isolations, competency, equipment, and emergency arrangements.\n3. Evaluate preventive and mitigative barriers for independence and current health.\n4. Stop or suspend work when a critical control is absent, failed, or unverifiable.\n5. Record accountable actions, revalidation triggers, and evidence required for safe closure.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.safety.validate-controls`\n- `nx.safety.inspect-permit`\n- `nx.safety.dispatch-emergency`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["hazard and task","people exposed","controls and barriers","site conditions","emergency authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.safety.validate-controls","nx.safety.inspect-permit","nx.safety.dispatch-emergency"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-orchestrate-emergency-response/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_industrial_security_commander","nx_physical_security_director","nx_soc_ot_fusion_director","nx_access_intelligence_lead","nx_cctv_intelligence_lead","nx_crisis_response_commander","nx_emergency_management_director","nx_hse_assurance_director","nx_investigations_evidence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-build-bowtie-analysis","name_ar":"بناء تحليل ربطة العنق","name_en":"Build Bowtie Analysis","description":"Execute build bowtie analysis for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to map threats, top event, consequences, preventive barriers, mitigative barriers, and degradation factors.","category":"hse-emergency","instructions_md":"# Build Bowtie Analysis\n\n**الاسم العربي:** بناء تحليل ربطة العنق  \n**المجال:** السلامة والطوارئ\n\n## Mission\n\nMap threats, top event, consequences, preventive barriers, mitigative barriers, and degradation factors. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- hazard and task\n- people exposed\n- controls and barriers\n- site conditions\n- emergency authority\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the task, hazard, exposed people, location, timing, and credible worst case.\n2. Verify prerequisite permits, isolations, competency, equipment, and emergency arrangements.\n3. Evaluate preventive and mitigative barriers for independence and current health.\n4. Stop or suspend work when a critical control is absent, failed, or unverifiable.\n5. Record accountable actions, revalidation triggers, and evidence required for safe closure.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.safety.validate-controls`\n- `nx.safety.inspect-permit`\n- `nx.safety.dispatch-emergency`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["hazard and task","people exposed","controls and barriers","site conditions","emergency authority"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.safety.validate-controls","nx.safety.inspect-permit","nx.safety.dispatch-emergency"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-build-bowtie-analysis/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-