fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.governance.list-controls`\n- `nx.governance.map-evidence`\n- `nx.governance.open-finding`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["applicable scope","control or legal requirement","process evidence","owner","assessment date"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.governance.list-controls","nx.governance.map-evidence","nx.governance.open-finding"],"risk_level":"high","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-perform-privacy-impact-assessment/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_pdpl_privacy_officer","nx_nca_ecc_assurance_lead","nx_iso27001_auditor","nx_iso45001_auditor","nx_iso55001_auditor","nx_hcis_compliance_lead","nx_third_party_risk_director","nx_records_governance_lead","nx_internal_audit_director"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-map-nca-ecc-controls","name_ar":"ربط ضوابط NCA ECC","name_en":"Map Nca Ecc Controls","description":"Execute map nca ecc controls for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to map implemented capabilities and evidence to current NCA ECC control objectives.","category":"compliance-privacy","instructions_md":"# Map Nca Ecc Controls\n\n**الاسم العربي:** ربط ضوابط NCA ECC  \n**المجال:** الامتثال والخصوصية\n\n## Mission\n\nMap implemented capabilities and evidence to current NCA ECC control objectives. Work from authoritative NEXI