ion, inference, and forecast.\n5. Return metric definitions, confidence, caveats, evidence queries, and owner actions.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.inspect-schema`\n- `nx.data.validate-quality`\n- `nx.data.trace-lineage`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["business question","data contract","source tables","quality thresholds","metric owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.inspect-schema","nx.data.validate-quality","nx.data.trace-lineage"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-detect-time-series-anomalies/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_data_steward","nx_analytics_insight_director","nx_semantic_layer_architect","nx_rag_knowledge_director","nx_ai_model_router","nx_agent_evaluation_director","nx_ai_safety_red_team_lead","nx_agent_memory_governor","nx_forecasting_science_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-build-causal-analysis","name_ar":"بناء تحليل سببي","name_en":"Build Causal Analysis","description":"Execute build causal analysis for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to form testable causal hypotheses, identify confounders, and avoid correlation-only claims.","category":"data-analytics","instructions_md":"# Build Causal Analysis\n\n**الاسم العربي:** بناء تحليل سببي  \n**المجال:** البيانات والتحليلات\n\n## Mission\n\nForm testable causal hypotheses, identify confounders, and avoid correlation-only claims. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- business question\n- data contract\n- source tables\n- quality thresholds\n- metric owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Restate the business question, grain, population, period, units, and decision use.\n2. Verify schema, lineage, access scope, freshness, completeness, and known exclusions.\n3. Test validity, uniqueness, consistency, distribution, and reconciliation controls.\n4. Calculate results reproducibly and distinguish observation, inference, and forecast.\n5. Return metric definitions, confidence, caveats, evidence queries, and owner actions.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.inspect-schema`\n- `nx.data.validate-quality`\n- `nx.data.trace-lineage`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["business question","data contract","source tables","quality thresholds","metric owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.inspect-schema","nx.data.validate-quality","nx.data.trace-lineage"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-build-causal-analysis/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-validate-executive-dashboard","name_ar":"التحقق من لوحة القيادة التنفيذية","name_en":"Validate Executive Dashboard","description":"Execute validate executive dashboard for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to verify KPI meaning, calculation, freshness, hierarchy, thresholds, and decision utility.","category":"data-analytics","instructions_md":"# Validate Executive Dashboard\n\n**الاسم العربي:** التحقق من لوحة القيادة التنفيذية  \n**المجال:** البيانات والتحليلات\n\n## Mission\n\nVerify KPI meaning, calculation, freshness, hierarchy, thresholds, and decision utility. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- business question\n- data contract\n- source tables\n- quality thresholds\n- metric owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Restate the business question, grain, population, period, units, and decision use.\n2. Verify schema, lineage, access scope, freshness, completeness, and known exclusions.\n3. Test validity, uniqueness, consistency, distribution, and reconciliation controls.\n4. Calculate results reproducibly and distinguish observation, inference, and forecast.\n5. Return metric definitions, confidence, caveats, evidence queries, and owner actions.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.inspect-schema`\n- `nx.data.validate-quality`\n- `nx.data.trace-lineage`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["business question","data contract","source tables","quality thresholds","metric owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.inspect-schema","nx.data.validate-quality","nx.data.trace-lineage"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-validate-executive-dashboard/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_chief_data_steward","nx_analytics_insight_director","nx_semantic_layer_architect","nx_rag_knowledge_director","nx_ai_model_router","nx_agent_evaluation_director","nx_ai_safety_red_team_lead","nx_agent_memory_governor","nx_forecasting_science_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-optimize-query-performance","name_ar":"تحسين أداء الاستعلامات","name_en":"Optimize Query Performance","description":"Execute optimize query performance for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to diagnose query cost, plans, indexes, cardinality, caching, and workload impact.","category":"data-analytics","instructions_md":"# Optimize Query Performance\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تحسين أداء الاستعلامات  \n**المجال:** البيانات والتحليلات\n\n## Mission\n\nDiag