proval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["task and risk tier","model and prompt version","tool policy","evaluation set","trace evidence"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.ai.evaluate-response","nx.ai.detect-prompt-injection","nx.agents.evaluate-run"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-detect-model-hallucination/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-govern-synthetic-data","name_ar":"حوكمة البيانات الاصطناعية","name_en":"Govern Synthetic Data","description":"Execute govern synthetic data for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to control provenance, privacy, representativeness, labeling, leakage, and allowed use.","category":"ai-agentic","instructions_md":"# Govern Synthetic Data\n\n**الاسم العربي:** حوكمة البيانات الاصطناعية  \n**المجال:** الذكاء الاصطناعي والوكلاء\n\n## Mission\n\nControl provenance, privacy, representativeness, labeling, leakage, and allowed use. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- task and risk tier\n- model and prompt version\n- tool policy\n- evaluation set\n- trace evidence\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Classify the use case, impact, autonomy, data sensitivity, and required human authority.\n2. Fix model, prompt, tools, retrieval corpus, policy, and evaluation versions.\n3. Run normal, edge, adversarial, and tool-misuse tests with trace capture.\n4. Measure task quality, grounding, safety, latency, cost, and approval compliance.\n5. Gate deployment on thresholds; document residual risk, monitoring, rollback, and owner.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.ai.evaluate-response`\n- `nx.ai.detect-prompt-injection`\n- `nx.agents.evaluate-run`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["task and risk tier","model and prompt version","tool policy","evaluation set","trace evidence"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.ai.evaluate-response","nx.ai.detect-prompt-injection","nx.agents.evaluate-run"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-govern-synthetic-data/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_multi_agent_orchestrator","nx_a2a_interoperability_gateway","nx_mcp_capability_broker","nx_tool_risk_controller","nx_human_approval_coordinator","nx_workflow_recovery_director","nx_evidence_provenance_agent","nx_observability_trace_agent","nx_continuous_improvement_agent"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-control-ai-cost","name_ar":"ضبط تكلفة الذكاء الاصطناعي","name_en":"Control Ai Cost","description":"Execute control ai cost for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to attribute token and tool cost, detect waste, enforce budgets, and preserve service quality.","category":"ai-agentic","instructions_md":"# Control Ai Cost\n\n**الاسم العربي:** ضبط تكلفة الذكاء الاصطناعي  \n**المجال:** الذكاء الاصطناعي والوكلاء\n\n## Mission\n\nAttribute token and tool cost, detect waste, enforce budgets, and preserve service quality. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- task and risk tier\n- model and prompt version\n- tool policy\n- evaluation set\n- trace evidence\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Classify the use case, impact, autonomy, data sensitivity, and required human authority.\n2. Fix model, prompt, tools, retrieval corpus, policy, and evaluation versions.\n3. Run normal, edge, adversarial, and tool-misuse tests with trace capture.\n4. Measure task quality, grounding, safety, latency, cost, and approval compliance.\n5. Gate deployment on thresholds; document residual risk, monitoring, rollback, and owner.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.ai.evaluate-response`\n- `nx.ai.detect-prompt-injection`\n- `nx.agents.evaluate-run`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["task and risk tier","model and prompt version","tool policy","evaluation set","trace evidence"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.ai.evaluate-response","nx.ai.detect-prompt-injection","nx.agents.evaluate-run"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-control-ai-cost/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-record-architecture-decision","name_ar":"توثيق قرار معماري","name_en":"Record Architecture Decision","description":"Execute record architecture decision for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to record context, options, decision, consequences, assumptions, and review triggers.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Record Architecture Decision\n\n**الاسم العربي:** توثيق قرار معماري  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nRecord context, options, decision, consequences, assumptions, and review triggers. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the change boundary, affected users, data, dependencies, and failure modes.\n2. Review design and implementation against explicit security and reliability invariants.\n3. Verify automated tests, migration safety, observability, performance, and rollback.\n4. Test high-risk paths and negative cases using reproducible evidence.\n5. Issue a release decision with blockers, owners, conditions, and post-deploy checks.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run`\n- `nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies`\n- `nx.observability.query-traces`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-record-architecture-decision/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_enterprise_architecture_director","nx_platform_engineering_lead","nx_sre_operations_lead","nx_devsecops_release_director","nx_quality_engineering_lead","nx_accessibility_quality_lead","nx_performance_engineering_lead","nx_database_reliability_lead","nx_integration_architecture_lead","nx_multi_agent_orchestrator","nx_a2a_interoperability_gateway","nx_mcp_capability_broker","nx_tool_risk_controller","nx_human_approval_coordinator","nx_workflow_recovery_director","nx_evidence_provenance_agent","nx_observability_trace_agent","nx_continuous_improvement_agent"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-review-api-contract","name_ar":"مراجعة عقد API","name_en":"Review Api Contract","description":"Execute review api contract for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to validate semantics, schema, authentication, compatibility, errors, idempotency, and observability.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Review Api Contract\n\n**الاسم العربي:** مراجعة عقد API  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nValidate semantics, schema, authentication, compatibility, errors, idempotency, and observability. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the change boundary, affected users, data, dependencies, and failure modes.\n2. Review design and implementation against explicit security and reliability invariants.\n3. Verify automated tests, migration safety, observability, performance, and rollback.\n4. Test high-risk paths and negative cases using reproducible evidence.\n5. Issue a release decision with blockers, owners, conditions, and post-deploy checks.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run`\n- `nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies`\n- `nx.observability.query-traces`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-review-api-contract/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-validate-database-migration","name_ar":"التحقق من ترحيل قاعدة البيانات","name_en":"Validate Database Migration","description":"Execute validate database migration for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to test locking, data preservation, reversibility, RLS, indexes, and deployment order.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Validate Database Migration\n\n**الاسم العربي:** التحقق من ترحيل قاعدة البيانات  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nTest locking, data preservation, reversibility, RLS, indexes, and deployment order. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark eac