en the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-audit-row-level-security/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-build-application-threat-model","name_ar":"بناء نموذج تهديد للتطبيق","name_en":"Build Application Threat Model","description":"Execute build application threat model for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to identify assets, trust boundaries, abuse cases, controls, and residual risk.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Build Application Threat Model\n\n**الاسم العربي:** بناء نموذج تهديد للتطبيق  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nIdentify assets, trust boundaries, abuse cases, controls, and residual risk. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the change boundary, affected users, data, dependencies, and failure modes.\n2. Review design and implementation against explicit security and reliability invariants.\n3. Verify automated tests, migration safety, observability, performance, and rollback.\n4. Test high-risk paths and negative cases using reproducible evidence.\n5. Issue a release decision with blockers, owners, conditions, and post-deploy checks.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run`\n- `nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies`\n- `nx.observability.query-traces`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-build-application-threat-model/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_enterprise_architecture_director","nx_platform_engineering_lead","nx_sre_operations_lead","nx_devsecops_release_director","nx_quality_engineering_lead","nx_accessibility_quality_lead","nx_performance_engineering_lead","nx_database_reliability_lead","nx_integration_architecture_lead","nx_multi_agent_orchestrator","nx_a2a_interoperability_gateway","nx_mcp_capability_broker","nx_tool_risk_controller","nx_human_approval_coordinator","nx_workflow_recovery_director","nx_evidence_provenance_agent","nx_observability_trace_agent","nx_continuous_improvement_agent"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-review-secure-code","name_ar":"مراجعة الكود الآمن","name_en":"Review Secure Code","description":"Execute review secure code for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to review changed code for exploitable behavior, authorization, data exposure, and unsafe defaults.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Review Secure Code\n\n**الاسم العربي:** مراجعة الكود الآمن  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nReview changed code for exploitable behavior, authorization, data exposure, and unsafe defaults. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the change boundary, affected users, data, dependencies, and failure modes.\n2. Review design and implementation against explicit security and reliability invariants.\n3. Verify automated tests, migration safety, observability, performance, and rollback.\n4. Test high-risk paths and negative cases using reproducible evidence.\n5. Issue a release decision with blockers, owners, conditions, and post-deploy checks.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run`\n- `nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies`\n- `nx.observability.query-traces`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"],"risk_level":"medium","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-review-secure-code/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-audit-dependency-risk","name_ar":"تدقيق مخاطر الاعتماديات","name_en":"Audit Dependency Risk","description":"Execute audit dependency risk for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to evaluate vulnerabilities, provenance, maintenance, licenses, transitive risk, and upgrade path.","category":"software-platform","instructions_md":"# Audit Dependency Risk\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تدقيق مخاطر الاعتماديات  \n**المجال:** هندسة البرمجيات والمنصة\n\n## Mission\n\nEvaluate vulnerabilities, provenance, maintenance, licenses, transitive risk, and upgrade path. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- change scope\n- architecture and code diff\n- test evidence\n- risk classification\n- rollback plan\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the change boundary, affected users, data, dependencies, and failure modes.\n2. Review design and implementation against explicit security and reliability invariants.\n3. Verify automated tests, migration safety, observability, performance, and rollback.\n4. Test high-risk paths and negative cases using reproducible evidence.\n5. Issue a release decision with blockers, owners, conditions, and post-deploy checks.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run`\n- `nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies`\n- `nx.observability.query-traces`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["change scope","architecture and code diff","test evidence","risk classification","rollback plan"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.devsecops.inspect-ci-run","nx.devsecops.scan-dependencies","nx.observability.query-traces"]