idate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["population and period","service or role","evidence sources","fairness constraints","accountable owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.communications.draft-mail"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-optimize-contact-center/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-detect-conduct-risk","name_ar":"كشف مخاطر السلوك","name_en":"Detect Conduct Risk","description":"Execute detect conduct risk for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to identify behavior and control patterns requiring fair, confidential human review.","category":"people-customer","instructions_md":"# Detect Conduct Risk\n\n**الاسم العربي:** كشف مخاطر السلوك  \n**المجال:** الموارد البشرية وتجربة العميل\n\n## Mission\n\nIdentify behavior and control patterns requiring fair, confidential human review. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- population and period\n- service or role\n- evidence sources\n- fairness constraints\n- accountable owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the population, outcome, period, legal or fairness constraints, and decision owner.\n2. Use aggregated evidence and minimize exposure of personal or sensitive data.\n3. Segment causes and needs without inferring protected traits or unsupported intent.\n4. Compare interventions by impact, fairness, feasibility, and measurement quality.\n5. Return accountable actions, communication, safeguards, and outcome measures.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["population and period","service or role","evidence sources","fairness constraints","accountable owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.communications.draft-mail"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-detect-conduct-risk/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":["nx_workforce_planning_director","nx_talent_intelligence_lead","nx_employee_experience_lead","nx_customer_experience_director","nx_service_recovery_lead","nx_communications_director","nx_sustainability_director","nx_procurement_value_director","nx_contract_intelligence_lead"],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-curate-enterprise-knowledge","name_ar":"تنسيق المعرفة المؤسسية","name_en":"Curate Enterprise Knowledge","description":"Execute curate enterprise knowledge for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to select, verify, structure, own, and retire knowledge for reliable reuse.","category":"people-customer","instructions_md":"# Curate Enterprise Knowledge\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تنسيق المعرفة المؤسسية  \n**المجال:** الموارد البشرية وتجربة العميل\n\n## Mission\n\nSelect, verify, structure, own, and retire knowledge for reliable reuse. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- population and period\n- service or role\n- evidence sources\n- fairness constraints\n- accountable owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Define the population, outcome, period, legal or fairness constraints, and decision owner.\n2. Use aggregated evidence and minimize exposure of personal or sensitive data.\n3. Segment causes and needs without inferring protected traits or unsupported intent.\n4. Compare interventions by impact, fairness, feasibility, and measurement quality.\n5. Return accountable actions, communication, safeguards, and outcome measures.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.data.query-catalog`\n- `nx.knowledge.search-corpus`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["population and period","service or role","evidence sources","fairness constraints","accountable owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.data.query-catalog","nx.knowledge.search-corpus","nx.communications.draft-mail"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-curate-enterprise-knowledge/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-write-bilingual-executive","name_ar":"كتابة تنفيذية ثنائية اللغة","name_en":"Write Bilingual Executive","description":"Execute write bilingual executive for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to produce aligned Arabic and English executive communication without semantic drift.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Write Bilingual Executive\n\n**الاسم العربي:** كتابة تنفيذية ثنائية اللغة  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nProduce aligned Arabic and English executive communication without semantic drift. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.knowledge.verify-citation`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n- `nx.documents.classify-document`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-write-bilingual-executive/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-review-arabic-rtl","name_ar":"مراجعة العربية واتجاه RTL","name_en":"Review Arabic Rtl","description":"Execute review arabic rtl for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to review language, typography, layout direction, numerals, controls, and mixed-script behavior.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Review Arabic Rtl\n\n**الاسم العربي:** مراجعة العربية واتجاه RTL  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nReview language, typography, layout direction, numerals, controls, and mixed-script behavior. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.knowledge.verify-citation`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n- `nx.documents.classify-document`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-review-arabic-rtl/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],