egulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-extract-meeting-actions/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-draft-stakeholder-brief","name_ar":"صياغة موجز أصحاب المصلحة","name_en":"Draft Stakeholder Brief","description":"Execute draft stakeholder brief for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to tailor a concise evidence-led brief to stakeholder priorities and concerns.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Draft Stakeholder Brief\n\n**الاسم العربي:** صياغة موجز أصحاب المصلحة  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nTailor a concise evidence-led brief to stakeholder priorities and concerns. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confiden