insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-localize-enterprise-content/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-create-incident-communication","name_ar":"إنشاء اتصال حادث","name_en":"Create Incident Communication","description":"Execute create incident communication for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to prepare timely, factual, approved incident updates for distinct audiences.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Create Incident Communication\n\n**الاسم العربي:** إنشاء اتصال حادث  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nPrepare timely, factual, approved incident updates for distinct audiences. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.knowledge.verify-citation`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n- `nx.documents.classify-document`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-create-incident-communication/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-summarize-long-documents","name_ar":"تلخيص الوثائق الطويلة","name_en":"Summarize Long Documents","description":"Execute summarize long documents for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to produce a faithful structured summary with decisions, obligations, risks, and citations.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Summarize Long Documents\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تلخيص الوثائق الطويلة  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nProduce a faithful structured summary with decisions, obligations, risks, and citations. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.knowledge.verify-citation`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n- `nx.documents.classify-document`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-summarize-long-documents/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}},{"id":"nx-design-decision-story","name_ar":"تصميم قصة القرار","name_en":"Design Decision Story","description":"Execute design decision story for NEXIOS with evidence, tenant isolation, explicit uncertainty, and governed actions. Use when the user or an agent needs to turn evidence into a transparent narrative from context to options, choice, and action.","category":"communication-experience","instructions_md":"# Design Decision Story\n\n**الاسم العربي:** تصميم قصة القرار  \n**المجال:** التواصل والتجربة\n\n## Mission\n\nTurn evidence into a transparent narrative from context to options, choice, and action. Work from authoritative NEXIOS evidence and return an auditable result that a human owner can verify.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- audience\n- communication purpose\n- source evidence\n- channel and length\n- approval owner\n\nBefore analysis, mark each input as verified, stale, missing, conflicting, or simulated. Record its source identifier and observation time.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the audience, required decision or behavior, channel, tone, and deadline.\n2. Extract only verified material claims and preserve uncertainty and source context.\n3. Structure the message for rapid comprehension, with Arabic as the primary language when requested.\n4. Review terminology, RTL behavior, accessibility, confidentiality, and approval requirements.\n5. Deliver the artifact with evidence references, owner, version, and follow-up action.\n6. Run a final contradiction, completeness, tenant-boundary, and approval check.\n\n## Evidence rules\n\n- Cite a source identifier and observation time for every material factual claim.\n- Separate fact, inference, forecast, recommendation, and human decision.\n- Use calibrated confidence: high, medium, low, or insufficient evidence.\n- Abstain when evidence is insufficient for a consequential conclusion.\n- Never treat simulated or demo data as production evidence.\n\n## Tool policy\n\nRecommended allowlist:\n- `nx.knowledge.verify-citation`\n- `nx.communications.draft-mail`\n- `nx.documents.classify-document`\n\nDiscover and call only tools approved for the active organization and agent. Validate input and output schemas. A tool descriptor does not prove that a connector is configured.\n\n## Approval and safety\n\n- Keep all access inside the active organization; never infer or combine cross-tenant data.\n- Request human approval before any write, notification, dispatch, account, financial, safety, or other material external action.\n- For life safety, security, legal, regulatory, medical, or financial consequences, provide decision support and route authority to the accountable human.\n- Do not bypass RLS, connector scopes, approval ledgers, rate limits, or audit logging.\n- Prefer reversible or compensating actions and state rollback criteria before execution.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn:\n\n1. `status`: complete, partial, blocked, or insufficient_evidence.\n2. `summary_ar`: concise Arabic-first result.\n3. `summary_en`: aligned English summary.\n4. `evidence`: source, source ID, observation time, supported claim, and confidence.\n5. `analysis`: method, comparisons, assumptions, and contradictions.\n6. `recommendations`: ranked options with benefits, risks, and dependencies.\n7. `actions`: owner, due date, approval requirement, and success measure.\n8. `confidence`: calibrated overall confidence and why.\n9. `limitations`: missing evidence, scope exclusions, and required expert review.\n\n## Completion gate\n\nComplete only when the result is reproducible from cited evidence, material uncertainty is visible, every consequential action has an owner and approval path, and no unresolved tenant or safety violation remains.\n","input_contract":{"required":["audience","communication purpose","source evidence","channel and length","approval owner"],"rules":["Identify the authoritative source and observation time for each material input.","State missing, stale, conflicting, or simulated data before analysis.","Minimize personal and sensitive data to the task purpose."]},"output_contract":{"format":"structured_markdown_and_json","required":["status","summary_ar","summary_en","evidence","analysis","recommendations","actions","confidence","limitations"],"evidenceItem":["source","source_id","observed_at","claim_supported","confidence"],"actionItem":["action","owner","due_at","approval_required","success_measure"]},"tool_allowlist":["nx.knowledge.verify-citation","nx.communications.draft-mail","nx.documents.classify-document"],"risk_level":"low","enabled":false,"version":1,"metadata":{"pack":"nexios-modern-skills-pack","path":"skills/nx-design-decision-story/SKILL.md","recommendedAgents":[],"sourceType":"original-derived-from-open-standards","importedAt":"2026-07-24T12:00:00+03:00"}}]
$skills$::jsonb) AS x(
    id text,
    name_ar text,
    name_en text,
    description text,
    category text,
    instructions_md text,
    input_contract jsonb,
    output_contract jsonb,
    tool_allowlist jsonb,
    risk_level text,
    enabled boolean,
    version integer,
    metadata jsonb
  )
)
INSERT INTO public.skill_registry (
  id, name_ar, name_en, description, category, instructions_md,
  input_contract, output_contract, tool_allowlist, risk_level,
  enabled, version, metadata
)
SELECT
  x.id, x.name_ar, x.name_en, x.description, x.category, x.instructions_md,
  x.input_contract, x.output_contract,
  ARRAY(SELECT jsonb_array_elements_text(x.tool_allowlist)),
  x.risk_level, false, x.version, x.metadata
FROM pack_rows x
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

COMMENT ON TABLE public.skill_registry IS
  'Governed NEXIOS skill instructions. Global definitions; per-organization activation is stored separately.';
COMMENT ON TABLE public.organization_skill_settings IS
  'Explicit tenant-scoped activation and configuration for NEXIOS skills.';
